  "answer": "The storefront is dropping specials that have an end date. I\u2019ll follow the debugging skill and trace that path before changing anything.The admin mapper writes the special\u2019s end date into the start-date field, and the price calculator then requires the start date to be both before and after today. I\u2019ll add tests for those two cases first.Creating a product through the admin API stored a special\u2019s end date in the start-date field, and the storefront price calculator then required that start date to be both before and after today, so any special with an end date never counted as a discount. The mapper now writes the end date onto the end-date field, and the calculator checks that the end date is still in the future.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am test -Dtest=ProductPriceUtilsDiscountTest,PersistableProductAvailabilityMapperTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\"], \"result\": \"passed\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"full storefront API against a running Shopizer instance\"], \"missing\": [\"an integration fixture that creates a product special through the admin REST API and reads it back from the storefront API\"]}",
